  "Question": "Which of the following properties does a rectangle have that a general parallelogram does not necessarily have?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Opposite sides are equal in length",
    "B": "The diagonals bisect each other",
    "C": "The diagonals are equal in length",
    "D": "Opposite angles are equal"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Equal opposite sides, equal opposite angles, and diagonals that bisect each other are properties of all parallelograms. Equal diagonals are a special property of rectangles.",
